node_modules
coverage
dist

# Vendored third-party text: this file IS the pin the OKF preset was derived
# from, so it must stay byte-identical to upstream. Formatting it would silently
# move the pin.
docs/okf/SPEC-v0.2.md

# Verbatim session transcripts, extracted mechanically from the session log.
# Reformatting one would silently alter the record it exists to preserve.
docs/workshop/**/raw.md

# Vendored material for repositories that do not exist yet. Formatting it here would
# apply this repo's style to files whose style is part of what a run is measured on.
.agents/skills/prepare-ablation-run/assets/**


# Conformance cases whose frontmatter block is deliberately defective -- a flow
# sequence that never closes, a fence that never closes, a block that parses to a
# list. Formatting would repair the exact defects they exist to present: prettier
# reads a lone `---` as a thematic break and inserts a blank line after it.
fixtures/conformance/frontmatter/docs/plain/broken/**

# The rejected-config tier: config bytes a load must refuse, and some of them
# are refused precisely because they are not YAML. Formatting one would repair
# the fault the case exists to state, on the same grounds as the broken
# frontmatter blocks above. Scoped to the tier directory rather than to the
# files that fail today, because which malformed shapes survive `--write` is an
# accident of the parser rather than a property anyone chose.
fixtures/conformance/rejected-config/**

# The body-structure tier: headings ARE the bytes under test. Prettier converts
# setext headings to ATX, strips closing hashes and trailing whitespace, and
# escapes `#Title`, so formatting would change what each case states and the
# tier would go green over a corpus nobody wrote. Scoped to the tier directory,
# not to today's offending files, on the same grounds as the entries above.
fixtures/conformance/body-structure/**

# The integrated tier holds no byte trick, but its cases are whole-corpus and its
# `expected-check.json` and `expected-query.json` are frozen, and lint-staged runs
# `prettier --write` on every staged `.md` and `.json`. Ignoring the directory
# keeps the commit hook from reformatting a frozen file.
fixtures/conformance/integrated/**

# Eval run output: gitignored, and must not be reformatted or checked.
evals/runs/
